  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-07T02:52:42.158Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "i have friends with worlds that have a lot of statues of their friends. as you can imagine this can make a world get large. it would make a lot of sense to have a vrc statue object/element in the sdk. this way, worlds with statues could be optimized to the point of not needing to include the avatar model itself. simply add the vrc statue object to your world, assign a username, and it will pull the users \"profile avatar\" from their account. this profile avatar would be something that each user can set, like a display picture. when a vrc statue requests the avatar of a user, it pulls the profile avatar of said user, from vrchat, instead of the avatar needing to be included in the world itself. the avatar statues would simply load in after the world loads, have default particle limits, and animations/sounds off, to avoid people crashing worlds by changing their profile avatar.",
